define phrase crowd-craning
  The crowd is made up of people from every part of the city. Men and women,
  aristocrats and servants, merchants and beggars, all rubbing shoulders and
  craning to see.
end phrase

define phrase crowd-intent-on-the-market
  No one pays any attention to you. Everyone is too intent on getting to
  Lord's Market.
end phrase

define phrase crowd-intent-on-the-square
  No one pays any attention to you. Everyone is too intent on watching the
  scene unfold in the middle of the square.
end phrase

