## `story.ni:9800`, the raid begins. DAVID: "Jacqueline" is Fiona's word —
## §3g; carried as the source has it.

define phrase raid-begins
  Suddenly, someone pounds on the front door. The sobs freeze in your throat
  as a voice outside shouts, 'Open in the name of Baron Fossville!'

  Fiona looks horrified. 'It's the Baron!' she whispers. 'I didn't think he'd
  come here so soon... quick, Jacqueline! Go to the laundry room!'
end phrase

## `story.ni:9705-9713`

define phrase still-in-shock, stopping
  You try to leave, but you're still disoriented, light-headed, and the floor
  seems to tilt beneath your feet. 'Wait,' Fiona says gently, putting her
  hand on your shoulder and guiding you back to the bed. 'Just wait. Rest.
  You're still in shock.'
or
  You try to leave, but you're still disoriented, light-headed, and the floor
  seems to tilt beneath your feet.
end phrase

define phrase fiona-knows-all-about-it
  Widow Fiona nods and presses the letter back into your hand. 'I know,
  child,' she says, 'I know all about it. But there'll be time to speak more
  of that later.'
end phrase

